    "permission": "Seymour Duncan encourages sharing these wiring diagrams freely; commercial use requires prior written permission. LIMITATIONS: The source's bridge ground wire terminates at the grounded tone casing, but this model has no bridge terminal. The generic four-conductor humbucker represents the series/parallel topology, not Seymour Duncan lead colors or physical switch-lug orientation. Pot lug orientation is logical rather than physical."
